                text: "The parts that make a vehicle ride, steer and meet emission rules: **Tenneco** (truck and car exhausts and Monroe shock absorbers), **Sharda Motor** (car and light-truck exhausts), **Gabriel** (shock absorbers, now also the Anand group's holding company), **JTEKT India** (electric and manual steering for Maruti and Toyota) and **Rane (Madras)** (steering gears, brake linings and valves). These are engineered with the vehicle maker years ahead of launch and rarely re-sourced mid-model, so **shares are high and sticky**. Exhausts gain from each new emission rule but have no place in a pure EV; steering and dampers go into every vehicle.",
