        salesDrivers: ["**New emission and fuel-efficiency rules**: CAFE III and BS6.3 from April 2027, then BS-VII, add an estimated ₹1,300–1,400cr of exhaust content over three to five years; hybrids need 1.5–2 times a petrol car's exhaust.", "**Ride control winning new cars**: the DaVinci damper won a flagship Mahindra SUV and four new customers in Q1, and a smaller version (DCx32) opens small cars; ride control grew 27.9% in Q1.", "**Truck and SUV volumes**: its biggest customers make trucks and SUVs, not small cars, which is why it grew slower than car production after the GST cut. ICRA expects truck volumes to fall in H2 FY27.", "**New plants**: plants run above 80% (clean air) and 90% (ride control). FY27 capex of ₹350–450cr, about three times FY26's ₹115cr and including two new plants for ₹140cr, is paid from its own cash and should earn about ₹3 of revenue per ₹1 spent at peak in FY28–FY29.", "**Exports**: 14–20% of the order book against 5–7% of sales today, with critical mass expected around 2028; US tariffs and weak Europe could slow it."],
